fficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to bring in some facts to discuss. Perhaps discuss Candidate D or A. Or we could weigh B vs C further. We could bring up B's weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy) and nasty remarks (crew cooperation). Also D's hot temper and know-it-all (communication). A's not open to new ideas (adaptability) and show-off (crew cooperation). So we could argue that B's concerns (nasty remarks) are serious, maybe outweigh his strengths. Or we could bring up D's strengths (responsibility, concentration) and concerns (hot temper). Or we could bring up C's stress resilience (keeps calm in crisis) and technical competence (understands complicated technology). That addresses missing data for C. Indeed we have note: C keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology. That is relevant to stress resilience and technical competence. So we can bring that to fill gap. That would strengthen C. So we could argue that C does have stress resilience and technical competence, contrary to earlier claim of missing data. So we could challenge Agent 3's view that C lacks evidence. Provide those facts. Then we can argue that C's reliability and decision quality plus now proven stress resilience and technical competence make C strong, while B's communication issues and weak memory for numbers are concerning. So we might shift recommendation back to C.\n\nThus as agent 2, we can bring those facts: C keeps calm in a crisis (stress resilience) and understands complicated technology (technical competence). Also note B's weak memory for numbers (attention) and nasty remarks (crew cooperation). So we can argue that C is stronger overall.\n\nThus we should state our current recommendation: Candidate C. Provide reasoning referencing Agent 1 and Agent 3 discussion, and our new facts.\n\nLet's craft public message: \"I agree with Agent 1 on C's reliability, and I can add that we have evidence C keeps calm in a crisis and understands complicated technology, addressing the stress resilience and technical competence gaps noted. Meanwhile B has weak memory for numbers and makes nasty remarks, which affect attention and crew cooperation. Therefore I maintain my recommendation for Candidate C.\"\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
