stion) and round 2 (public message supporting C). Now round 3 we need to respond again. We need to follow meeting process: make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, providing evidence, and state current recommendation. We need to decide whether to maintain C or shift. The current state: Agent 1 and Agent 2 both recommend C, Agent 3 now recommends C (just changed). So all three now recommend C. So we can reaffirm C, maybe bring in additional evidence about other candidates (A, D) to confirm C is best. We should reference prior discussion and maybe bring new facts about A and D to show they are less suitable. Provide evidence: A not open to new ideas, show-off, unfriendly, not open to new ideas, etc. D has hot temper, know-it-all, moody, loner. So we can argue that those concerns make them less suitable. So we reaffirm C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I continue to recommend Candidate C...\" referencing evidence: reliability, quick decisions, calm in crisis, understands technology, positive crew atmosphere, and note that A and D have significant concerns (A not open to new ideas, show-off, unfriendly; D hot temper, know-it-all, moody). Also note B's weak memory and nasty remarks. So C is best.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\":\"agent_2\",\"vote\":\"Candidate C\"}\n\nProceed."}
